{
  "_source_notes": {
    "source": "SRD 5.1 Weapons table and Armor table, transcribed in full.",
    "conventions": [
      "cost and weight are kept as literal strings matching the SRD table's own units (sp/gp/cp, lb.) rather than converted to a single numeric unit.",
      "damage is split into count/sides/type for weapons, matching the convention already used in weapons.json.",
      "properties are the raw SRD property strings for each weapon, including any range or versatile-damage annotation exactly as printed.",
      "armor AC is given both as the literal SRD string and as structured fields (base, dexCap) for code use: dexCap is null for light armor (full Dex, uncapped), 2 for medium armor, and 0 for heavy armor (no Dex at all).",
      "material is a string array of physical materials for rules hooks (e.g. Shocking Grasp). Metal armors include \"metal\"; leather/hide/padded and shields use an empty array.",
      "strengthRequirement is null unless the SRD lists a minimum Strength score. stealthDisadvantage is true only where the table marks Disadvantage."
    ]
